---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code as CodeSnippet } from "astro:components";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Section Summary: Selection</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-4" />

        <p class="text-secondary">
          Activities 1.11 &ndash; 1.16. Use this to review, or to fill in a definition you missed.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">1.</span> Booleans and Comparison</h2>

          <p>
            A comparison produces a boolean, and
            a boolean can be stored like any other value. One{" "}
            <CodeSnippet code="=" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline
            /> assigns; three ask whether two values match.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Comparison operator</dt>
            <dd>
            A symbol that compares two values and produces a boolean.
            </dd>
            <dt>Boolean expression</dt>
            <dd>
            A piece of code that evaluates to <CodeSnippet code="true" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline /> or <CodeSnippet code="false" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />.
            </dd>
            <dt>Assignment</dt>
            <dd>
            Putting a value into a variable, written with a single{" "}
            <CodeSnippet code="=" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />.
            </dd>
            <dt>Equality</dt>
            <dd>
            Asking whether two values match, written with{" "}
            <CodeSnippet code="===" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />.
            </dd>
            <dt>
            <CodeSnippet code="confirm()" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />
            </dt>
            <dd>
            Asks the user a yes-or-no question and returns a boolean.
            Only <CodeSnippet code="y" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline /> or{" "}
            <CodeSnippet code="Y" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline /> means{" "}
            <CodeSnippet code="true" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">2.</span> Making Decisions</h2>

          <p>
            An{" "}
            <CodeSnippet code="if" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline
            /> statement runs a block only when its condition is true. Without
            one, statements simply run in order.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Selection</dt>
            <dd>
            Choosing which code to run based on a condition.
            </dd>
            <dt>Condition</dt>
            <dd>
            The boolean expression that decides which path is taken.
            </dd>
            <dt>Block</dt>
            <dd>
            The group of statements inside a pair of braces.
            </dd>
            <dt>Sequencing</dt>
            <dd>
            Running statements one after another, in order.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">3.</span> Chains of Decisions</h2>

          <p>
            In a chain, the first true condition
            wins and the rest are skipped. Order the conditions carelessly and
            some of them can never run at all.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Chain</dt>
            <dd>
            A series of conditions where the first true one runs and the
            rest are skipped.
            </dd>
            <dt>Branch</dt>
            <dd>One possible path through a decision.</dd>
            <dt>Unreachable code</dt>
            <dd>
            Code that can never run, no matter what the input is.
            </dd>
            <dt>Mutually exclusive</dt>
            <dd>
            Outcomes where only one can happen at a time.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">4.</span> p5 Lab 3: Decisions You Can See</h2>

          <p>
            The same conditions, with
            the result on screen instead of in the console &mdash; a color
            chosen by a value, or a shape stopped at an edge.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Clamp</dt>
            <dd>
            To limit a value so it cannot go past a maximum or minimum.
            </dd>
            <dt>Boundary</dt>
            <dd>
            A limit that a condition tests against, such as the edge of
            the canvas.
            </dd>
            <dt>State</dt>
            <dd>
            The current values a program is holding, which decide what it
            draws.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">5.</span> Combining Conditions</h2>

          <p>
            Two conditions can be joined into one
            with AND and OR, or reversed with NOT. Read a compound condition
            left to right and ask what has to be true.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Logical operator</dt>
            <dd>
            An operator that combines or reverses boolean values:{" "}
            <CodeSnippet code="&&" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />, <CodeSnippet code="||" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />, <CodeSnippet code="!" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />.
            </dd>
            <dt>Compound condition</dt>
            <dd>A condition built from two or more simpler conditions.</dd>
            <dt>Negation</dt>
            <dd>Reversing a boolean value.</dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">6.</span> Nested Conditions and Randomness</h2>

          <p>
            A conditional inside
            another asks a follow-up question, one that only makes sense when
            the first answer was yes.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Nested conditional</dt>
            <dd>A conditional written inside another conditional's block.</dd>
            <dt>Nesting depth</dt>
            <dd>How many levels deep a piece of code sits.</dd>
            <dt>
            <CodeSnippet code="Math.floor()" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />
            </dt>
            <dd>Rounds a decimal down to the whole number below it.</dd>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  dl {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  dt {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  dd {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
  section {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
</style>
